{"name":"Nacho Cheese","hex":"#ffbb00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nacho cheese","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A processed cheese sauce mixed with peppers and spices, most often eaten with nachos."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nacho_cheese"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nachos","blocks":[{"text":"Nachos are a Tex-Mex dish consisting of tortilla chips or totopos covered with cheese or chile con queso, as well as a variety of other toppings and garnishes, often including meats, vegetables, and condiments such as salsa, guacamole, or sour cream. At its most basic form, nachos may consist of merely chips covered with melted cheese, or cheese sauce and served as an appetizer or snack, while other versions are substantial enough to serve as a main course. The dish was created by, and named after, Mexican restaurateur Ignacio \"Nacho\" Anaya, who created it in 1943 for American customers at the Victory Club restaurant in Piedras Negras, Coahuila."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Nachos-cheese.jpg/330px-Nachos-cheese.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nachos","wikidata":"Q466430"},{"title":"Cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheese is a type of dairy product produced in a range of flavors, textures, and forms by curdling of milk, usually from cows, goats or sheep, and sometimes of water buffalo. During production, milk is usually acidified and either the enzymes of rennet or bacterial enzymes with similar activity are added to cause the protein casein to coagulate. The solid curds, consisting of proteins and milkfat, are then separated from the liquid whey and pressed into finished cheese. Some cheeses have aromatic molds on the outer layer or rind, while others have them throughout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Cheese_platter.jpg/330px-Cheese_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese","wikidata":"Q10943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Nachos_with_chicken%2C_with_salsa_and_jalapenos_on_the_side.jpg/500px-Nachos_with_chicken%2C_with_salsa_and_jalapenos_on_the_side.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Nachos_with_chicken%2C_with_salsa_and_jalapenos_on_the_side.jpg/1280px-Nachos_with_chicken%2C_with_salsa_and_jalapenos_on_the_side.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Nachos_with_chicken%2C_with_salsa_and_jalapenos_on_the_side.jpg/500px-Nachos_with_chicken%2C_with_salsa_and_jalapenos_on_the_side.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nachos with chicken, with salsa and jalapenos on the side","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANachos_with_chicken%2C_with_salsa_and_jalapenos_on_the_side.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/NachosWithBeefAndBeans.jpg/500px-NachosWithBeefAndBeans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/NachosWithBeefAndBeans.jpg/1280px-NachosWithBeefAndBeans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/NachosWithBeefAndBeans.jpg/500px-NachosWithBeefAndBeans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nachos with beef and beans in a skillet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANachosWithBeefAndBeans.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Nachos.2.jpg/500px-Nachos.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, ht